THIRD-PARTY DATA INCLUDED IN THE REPOSITORY

web/src/sky/stardata.js holds data from two sources.

1. The star distances in that file (the fifth number of each star) come
from the HYG database v4.1 by astronexus
(https://github.com/astronexus/HYG-Database, file
hyg/CURRENT/hygdata_v41.csv; the database is now kept at
https://codeberg.org/astronexus/hyg), which takes them from the Hipparcos
parallaxes. HYG is licensed under the Creative Commons
Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International License
(http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/). Changes made: only the
distance column is kept, matched to the stars by Hipparcos number, rounded
to a tenth of a parsec, with 0 written for an unknown distance. Those
distance values remain under CC BY-SA 4.0; the Apache-2.0 licence of this
project does not replace it for them. The page uses the distances only to
show depth while the sky view is moving.

2. Everything else in that file (bright stars, star names and constellation
figures for the sky view) is derived from data files of d3-celestial
(https://github.com/ofrohn/d3-celestial), which take their positions from
the Hipparcos catalogue (ESA 1997). They are used under the BSD 3-Clause
